The plugin's session wizard was rewritten as a provider cell. What carried
over is the shape of the integration: one OpenAI-chat base named by the
configuration, the project key read from AIXY_API_KEY or saved through the
harness' own credential writer, the catalog read with one authenticated GET of
{base}/models (a redirect refused, so the key is never forwarded, and each id
listed once with the context length only when the gateway advertises one), the
base validated as HTTPS or loopback HTTP with no credentials, query or
fragment, and the X-Aixy-Session-ID header that groups a conversation in Aixy
Activity. The plugin's prompt-and-confirm flow is not code here: Nodecode's
/connect saves the key, /models and /setup pick the model, and /aixy reads the
gateway's catalog on demand. The optional MCP OAuth step of setup is left out,
because Nodecode's own mcp cell is what connects an MCP server; no wizard
state, no config rewriting of a foreign harness, and no dependencies are
carried over.
